.TH FREERAM 1 "January 2026" "freeram 2.0.0"
.SH NAME
freeram \- clear cached memory to free up RAM

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B freeram
[\fB\-y\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR]
[\fB\-\-stats\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B freeram
clears the filesystem cache to free up RAM on Linux systems.
It reads memory statistics, drops caches, and reports the amount of memory freed.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip confirmation prompt. Useful for scripts and automation.

.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-silent
Silent mode. No output unless an error occurs.

.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Test mode (dry run). Shows what would happen without actually clearing caches.

.TP
.BR \-\-stats
Display memory statistics and history.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this help message.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information.

.SH FILES

.TP
.I /var/log/freeram.log
Log file containing timestamped records of memory freed.

.TP
.I /var/lib/freeram/history
History file tracking all memory freeing operations.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Interactive mode:
.B sudo freeram

.TP
Non-interactive:
.B sudo freeram -y

.TP
Show statistics:
.B sudo freeram --stats

.TP
Dry run:
.B sudo freeram -t

.SH REQUIREMENTS
Root privileges (sudo)

.SH AUTHOR
Originally by mrprohack and tamilanmkv

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sync (1),
.BR drop_caches (7)
